{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"color"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/dot-swift.struct\/init(font:color:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion/Dot-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLTuplet.Portion.Dot","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Dot","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/dot-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion\/Dot-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tuplet-dot type is used to specify dotted tuplet types."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Dot","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion/Dot-swift.struct/init(font:color:)":{"title":"init(font:color:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/dot-swift.struct\/init(font:color:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion\/Dot-swift.struct\/init(font:color:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLTuplet.Portion.Dot"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion":{"title":"MXLTuplet.Portion","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Portion","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet\/Portion","abstract":[{"text":"The tuplet-portion type provides optional full control over tuplet specifications. It allows the number and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"note type (including dots) to be set for the actual and normal portions of a single tuplet. If any of these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements are absent, their values are based on the time-modification element."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Portion","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"typ